# Native App — Context

## Status
Active development. UI/UX polish in progress (Session 2026-08-19).

## Stack
- React Native + Expo (bare managed)
- NativeWind (TailwindCSS for RN) — theme classes (dark/light) applied via root `View className`
- Redux Toolkit + redux-persist
- React Hook Form + Zod
- react-native-toast-message (global `<Toaster />` in App.tsx; modals include own `<Toast />`)
- `@gym/shared` for DTO types

## Theme System
- 3 themes: `light`, `dark`, `amoled` — Redux `state.theme.theme`
- 4 style modes: `minimal`, `glass`, `clay`, `liquid-glass` — Redux `state.theme.styleMode`
- **Source of truth**: `global.css` CSS variables → Tailwind classes (`text-foreground`, `bg-background`, etc.)
- **For icons/inline styles only**: `useTheme().colors` object (synced with global.css)
- **Rule**: Use Tailwind semantic classes for all text/bg. Use `colors.xxx` only for lucide icon `color=` props and unavoidable inline styles.
- **Transparent overlays**: On image backgrounds use `text-white` / `text-white/60` directly (not theme tokens) — see Footer transparent mode.

## Key Files
- `App.tsx` — root navigator; `<Toaster />` and `<GlobalSettingsOverlay />` are outside navigator
- `global.css` — CSS variable definitions for all themes (light/dark/amoled)
- `tailwind.config.js` — maps CSS vars to Tailwind color tokens
- `src/hooks/useTheme.ts` — `colors` object for icon/inline use; also exports `isDark`, `theme`, `styleMode`
- `src/components/ui/Input.tsx` — theme-aware; uses `isDark` for bg rgba
- `src/components/ui/Card.tsx` — `bg-card border-border`; glass/clay/minimal/default variants
- `src/components/ui/SectionBackground.tsx` — full-bleed image bg with dark overlay; no horizontal fade bands
- `src/components/ui/Toaster.tsx` — global toast; positioned top-right, pushed left with `pr-24 md:pr-32` to avoid settings overlay overlap
- `src/components/layout/Footer.tsx` — supports `transparent` prop: forces `text-white`/`text-white/60` on image backgrounds
- `src/components/layout/AppDock.tsx` — renders `FloatingDock` (auth) or `PublicFloatingDock` (public)
- `src/components/layout/FloatingDock.tsx` — icon color uses `colors.mutedForeground` (not `colors.muted`) for inactive items
- `src/components/layout/PublicFloatingDock.tsx` — same icon fix; `colors.mutedForeground` for inactive
- `src/components/layout/GlobalSettingsOverlay.tsx` — positioned `right: 32` to avoid scrollbar overlap
- `src/components/layout/ScreenWrapper.tsx` — renders `<AppDock />` for screens inside the stack
- `src/pages/PublicHomeScreen.tsx` — renders own `<AppDock />` (not in ScreenWrapper); bottom section has no `bg-background` so image bleeds into footer
- `src/pages/MemberLoginScreen.tsx` — renders own `<AppDock />`
- `src/features/staff/staffApi.ts` — Plans endpoints: `/plans/workout-templates`, `/plans/diet-templates` (require auth token)
- `src/features/public/publicApi.ts` — `listPublicPlans()`, `submitPublicInquiry()` (no auth required)
- `src/features/members/memberApi.ts` — CRUD + QR + login
- `src/services/api.ts` — axios instance; base URL from `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` or AsyncStorage override

## AppDock Architecture
- **NOT global in App.tsx** — React Navigation requires `useRoute()` to be inside a screen
- `ScreenWrapper` renders `<AppDock />` for all internal screens
- `PublicHomeScreen` and `MemberLoginScreen` render `<AppDock />` directly (they don't use ScreenWrapper)
- **If adding new pages that don't use ScreenWrapper**, manually add `<AppDock />` at the bottom of the return

## Error Parsing Pattern (standard)
```ts
function parseApiError(error: any): string {
  const data = error?.response?.data;
  if (data?.message && typeof data.message === 'string') return data.message;
  if (Array.isArray(data?.message)) return data.message.join(', ');
  if (data?.error && typeof data.error === 'string') return data.error;
  if (error?.message && typeof error.message === 'string') return error.message;
  return 'An unexpected error occurred. Please try again.';
}
```

## ✅ Fixed This Session
1. **AppDock crashes** — `useRoute()` crash fixed: AppDock stays inside ScreenWrapper (not App.tsx root); public pages render their own AppDock
2. **Dock icon colors** — Changed `colors.muted` → `colors.mutedForeground` for inactive icons in both FloatingDock and PublicFloatingDock
3. **SectionBackground horizontal lines** — Removed top/bottom `bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-xl` bands
4. **Footer on image bg** — Footer uses `transparent` prop; text → `text-white`/`text-white/60`; seamlessly bleeds into last image section
5. **Toast position** — Pushed left with `pr-24 md:pr-32` to avoid settings icons overlap
6. **Settings overlay position** — Moved `right: 16` → `right: 32` to clear browser scrollbar
7. **Button layout shift** — Added explicit `minHeight` via inline `style` prop so loading spinner swap doesn't resize button
8. **Plans → auth-only** — Removed `Plans` nav item from `PublicFloatingDock`; public CTAs now navigate to `MemberLogin` or `Login`
9. **Homepage complete rework** — 3 seamless full-bleed `ImageBackground` sections (hero / experience / training + cta). No `bg-background` breaks. All text is white with opacity. Dark gradient overlays on each section. Feature chips use glassmorphism (`rgba(255,255,255,0.10)` bg + `border-white/15`). Footer embedded inside last section image. Contact form embedded in section 2 with translucent card.

## ⚠️ Still Needs Attention
- **Plans screen empty** — `PlansScreen` calls `/plans/workout-templates` which requires a staff auth Bearer token. Must be logged in as staff/admin.
- **Web CSS gradients** — `ImageBackground` on web doesn't support CSS `linear-gradient` in `style`. The gradient overlay currently uses a flat `rgba` fallback. For web, a proper `<View style={{ background: 'linear-gradient(...)' }}` overlay would be more accurate.
- **Remaining `colors.xxx` inline styles** — ~30 components still use legacy inline `colors.xxx` for text/bg instead of Tailwind classes (non-breaking).
- **Passkey flow** — Simulated (no real WebAuthn on mobile RN)
- **Staff creation UX** — Requires user UUID; no email-lookup endpoint

## Phone Prefix Pattern (MemberFormModal)
- Default: `+91`; combined: `${phonePrefix}${phone}` → `+919876543210`
- `extractPhoneNumber(fullPhone)` splits on edit mode

## Strong Password Regex
```
/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)(?=.*[@$!%*?&])[A-Za-z\d@$!%*?&]{8,}$/
```
